---
import Layout from "../../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import Hero from "../../../components/Hero.astro";
import Figure from "../../../components/Figure.astro";
import Icon from "../../../components/Icon.astro";
import { withBase } from "../../../consts";
import heroImg from "../../../assets/photos/fuji-musee-escaliers.jpg";
import itineraireImg from "../../../assets/photos/fuji-musee-itineraire-kawaguchiko.jpg";
import corvetteImg from "../../../assets/photos/fuji-musee-corvette-parking.jpg";
import salleImg from "../../../assets/photos/fuji-musee-salle-prototypes-toyota.jpg";
import plongeanteImg from "../../../assets/photos/fuji-musee-vue-plongeante-prototype.webp";
import ts050Img from "../../../assets/photos/fuji-musee-ts050-hybrid-lemans.jpg";
import indycarImg from "../../../assets/photos/fuji-musee-indycar-penske-marlboro.jpg";
import evoImg from "../../../assets/photos/fuji-musee-evo-rallye-marlboro.jpg";
import gtpImg from "../../../assets/photos/fuji-musee-gtp-salle-sombre.jpg";
import circuitImg from "../../../assets/photos/fuji-speedway-vue-brouillard.jpg";

const parkingMapsHref = "https://www.google.com/maps/search/?api=1&query=35.367995,138.918814";
---

<Layout
  title="Fuji Motor Sports Museum"
  description="The Fuji Motor Sports Museum, next to Fuji Speedway: how to get there, admission, parking and my review after the visit."
>
  <Hero
    image={heroImg}
    eyebrow="Great spot · Mount Fuji"
    title="Fuji Motor Sports Museum"
    subtitle="Next to Fuji Speedway, one of the finest collections of race cars in Japan."
  />

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 py-10 sm:py-14 sm:px-8">
    <a
      href={withBase("/en/mount-fuji/")}
      class="link-underline reveal inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 font-body text-sm font-medium text-ink-soft"
    >
      <Icon name="arrow-left" class="h-3.5 w-3.5" />
      Back to Mount Fuji
    </a>

    <p class="reveal mt-8 font-body text-lg leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      A few minutes from Fuji Speedway, the Fuji Motor Sports Museum wasn't part of my itinerary, and yet it turned out
      to be one of the best surprises of my time at Mount Fuji. Between Le Mans prototypes, historic single-seaters and
      rally cars, the collection has nothing to envy the biggest car museums. Here's how to get there and what to
      expect.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 pb-10 sm:pb-14 sm:px-8">
    <h2 class="reveal font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink sm:text-3xl">How to get there?</h2>

    <p class="reveal mt-6 font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      From Kawaguchiko, allow about 30 to 35 minutes by road. The drive is very pleasant, a real change from cities
      like Tokyo or Osaka, where red lights and traffic jams are part of the deal. You'll drive along the track and take
      small forest roads, perfect for testing your rental car if you've decided to treat yourself, or simply to visit
      and take great photos.
    </p>
    <p class="reveal mt-4 font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
      Once you arrive, a free, easy-to-access parking lot awaits. Admission to the museum is around €10.
    </p>

    <div class="reveal mt-6 rounded-lg border border-mist-200 bg-paper-dim/40 p-5">
      <p class="eyebrow text-racing-500">Fuji Motor Sports Museum</p>
      <p class="mt-2 font-body text-sm text-ink-soft">
        Free, easy-to-access parking, about 20 meters from the museum entrance.
      </p>
      <a
        href={parkingMapsHref}
        target="_blank"
        rel="noopener noreferrer"
        class="link-underline mt-3 inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 font-body text-sm font-medium text-racing-500"
      >
        Open in Google Maps
        <Icon name="external-link" class="h-3.5 w-3.5" />
      </a>
    </div>

    <Figure
      image={itineraireImg}
      alt="Google Maps screenshot of the driving route between Kawaguchiko and the museum, 35 minutes via the E68"
      caption="The drive from Kawaguchiko: 35 minutes, between lake and forest."
      class="mx-auto mt-8 max-w-xs sm:max-w-sm"
    />

    <Figure
      image={corvetteImg}
      alt="White Corvette C7 Stingray parked in the museum's free parking lot, in the rain"
      caption="My Corvette C7, parked in the museum's free parking lot."
      class="mt-8"
    />
    <a
      href={withBase("/en/mount-fuji/mfj-rental-cars/")}
      class="link-underline reveal mt-3 inline-flex w-fit items-center gap-1.5 font-body text-sm font-medium text-racing-500"
    >
      Want the same one? Here's how I rented it from MFJ Rental Cars
      <Icon name="arrow-right" class="h-3.5 w-3.5" />
    </a>
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-mist-200 bg-paper-dim/50 py-10 sm:py-14">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5 sm:px-8">
      <h2 class="reveal font-display text-2xl font-semibold text-ink sm:text-3xl">What to expect</h2>

      <p class="reveal mt-6 max-w-2xl font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        Without spoiling too much: the museum is spread over 2 floors. Rally cars, vintage Formula 1 cars and many other
        models await you. Guides and an audio guide are also available to tell you the story of each car. The
        atmosphere is really great, any enthusiast will have a blast.
      </p>

      <Figure
        image={salleImg}
        alt="Museum hall with several Toyota prototypes and race cars on display"
        caption="Under a soaring glass roof, the prototypes line up hall after hall."
        class="mt-8"
      />

      <div class="mt-6 grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2">
        <Figure
          image={plongeanteImg}
          alt="Bird's-eye view of a cream-colored Toyota race prototype, from an upper floor of the museum"
          caption="Looking down on a prototype, between two floors linked by escalators."
        />
        <Figure
          image={ts050Img}
          alt="Toyota TS050 Hybrid #8, winner of the 24 Hours of Le Mans, displayed with its hybrid powertrain"
          caption="The TS050 Hybrid, winner at the 24 Hours of Le Mans, still covered in race dust."
        />
        <Figure
          image={indycarImg}
          alt="Toyota IndyCar in Marlboro Team Penske colors, displayed next to another black Toyota IndyCar"
          caption="A Toyota IndyCar in Marlboro Team Penske colors, parked next to its FedEx rival."
        />
        <Figure
          image={evoImg}
          alt="Mitsubishi Lancer Evo rally car in Marlboro colors, rear view from the museum's mezzanine"
          caption="A Mitsubishi Lancer Evo rally car in Marlboro colors, in the upstairs gallery."
        />
      </div>

      <Figure
        image={gtpImg}
        alt="White Toyota GTP race prototype displayed in a dark hall of the museum"
        caption="Another hall, another atmosphere: this prototype keeps all its presence in the half-light."
        class="mx-auto mt-6 max-w-sm"
        aspectClass="aspect-[3/4]"
      />

      <p class="reveal mt-10 max-w-2xl font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        On the top floor, a gift shop sells miniature race cars, mugs, T-shirts, etc. (on the pricey side), plenty to
        treat yourself. There's also a café overlooking the track, a must if you've already driven it in a sim. And
        finally, a little surprise awaits the biggest Formula 1 fans ;)
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="py-10 sm:py-14">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 sm:px-8">
      <p class="reveal font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        As for me, in September, the weather was bad and I couldn't see the whole track. The museum experience was
        great, though.
      </p>
      <p class="reveal mt-4 font-body text-sm leading-relaxed text-ink-soft">
        The road leading to the track is superb, it reminds me of the one leading to the Spa-Francorchamps circuit in
        Belgium. The track is surrounded by dense forest, with an impressive view of Mount Fuji!
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="mx-auto max-w-5xl px-5 pb-10 sm:pb-14 sm:px-8">
    <Figure
      image={circuitImg}
      alt="View of the Fuji Speedway track in the fog, with a corner and Panasonic Automotive signs visible"
      caption="The Fuji Speedway track in the mist, right next to the museum."
    />
  </section>

  <section class="border-t border-mist-200 bg-paper-dim/50 py-10 sm:py-14">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-5 text-center sm:px-8">
      <a
        href={withBase("/en/mount-fuji/")}
        class="link-underline reveal inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 font-body text-sm font-medium text-ink"
      >
        <Icon name="arrow-left" class="h-3.5 w-3.5" />
        Back to all Mount Fuji spots
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
